# DRAW keymap preset: Microsoft Paint (Windows 10 / 11 default shortcuts)
#
# Format: actionId keycode requireMods forbidMods [device button]
#   mods bits: 1=Ctrl 2=Shift 4=Alt. forbidMods 0 = every modifier the row does not require
#   (Shift stays allowed on printable non-letters like > { + _ , typed with it).
#   A row that must leave Shift+key alone (Ctrl+] vs Ctrl+Shift+]) writes forbidMods 6.
#   Ctrl+Shift+punctuation is the UNshifted key with Ctrl+Shift: Ctrl+Shift+' = 39 3 (not 34).
#   Keycodes: letters are lowercase ASCII (Shift+letter = the letter, requireMods 2);
#   Tab 9, Backspace 8, Enter 13, Insert 20992, Delete 21248, F1 15104 ... F10 17408,
#   F11 34048, F12 34304. Action ids: GUI/COMMAND.BM (CMD_init) / SHORTCUTS.md.
# How a keymap applies (CFG/BINDINGS.BM BINDINGS_apply):
#   - an action's Nth row moves its Nth key; a row past the keys it has ADDS one
#   - a DRAW key a row takes is unbound (that DRAW action loses the key)
#   - keys no row takes keep their DRAW meaning
# Mac apps: Cmd is Ctrl here, Option is Alt.
# Paint's tools have no letter keys (it uses the ribbon), so DRAW's tool letters stay.
# Already the same in DRAW (no row): Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+Y undo / redo, Ctrl+A select all,
#   Ctrl+C / X / V, Delete clear the selection, F11 full-screen view (DRAW: hide all UI),
#   Ctrl+N / O / S, Ctrl+B / I / U bold / italic / underline while typing text.
# Not in DRAW (no row): Ctrl+P print, Ctrl+R rulers (stays Reference Image), Ctrl+L
#   layers (newer Paint; Ctrl+L stays Layer Panel), Alt+F4.
# DRAW keys this preset takes: Ctrl+PgUp / PgDn move layer (Paint: zoom), Ctrl+G new
#   group (Paint: gridlines), Ctrl+E clear selection (Delete still clears), Ctrl+W, F12
#   (developer dump / brush export). Ctrl+= / Ctrl+- become brush size, as in Paint.

406 18688 1 0   # Ctrl+PgUp     zoom in
407 20736 1 0   # Ctrl+PgDn     zoom out
602 93 0 0      # ]             (DRAW's own key, kept)
602 61 1 0      # Ctrl++  (Ctrl+=)  bigger brush / line
601 91 0 0      # [             (DRAW's own key, kept)
601 45 1 0      # Ctrl+-        smaller brush / line
8102 103 1 0    # Ctrl+G        gridlines          -> Pixel Grid
1801 101 1 0    # Ctrl+E        image properties (size) -> Resize Canvas
1805 119 1 0    # Ctrl+W        resize and skew    -> Resize Image with Content
1802 120 3 0    # Ctrl+Shift+X  crop               -> Crop Canvas
204 34304 0 0   # F12           save as
